Third-party tools the Collector runs
------------------------------------
The Collector does not contain these tools in its Python package. It runs them as
separate programs, and the Docker image and `risklence-scanner install-tools` put
them on a machine. Each keeps its own licence, which is not Apache-2.0:

- nmap (https://nmap.org). Licensed under the Nmap Public Source License (NPSL,
  https://nmap.org/npsl/), a licence of its own, not Apache-2.0 and not MIT. The
  NPSL has terms about redistributing nmap, including in a product or an image
  you distribute to others. Read it before you redistribute an image that
  contains nmap. The Collector's Docker image installs nmap from the Debian
  package archive.
- subfinder (https://github.com/projectdiscovery/subfinder). MIT licence. Pinned
  by `install-tools` at the version in
  `scanner_agent/tool_installer_constants.py`; the Docker image builds the
  version current at build time.
- nuclei (https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei). MIT licence. Pinned the
  same way as subfinder.
- nuclei-templates (https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates). MIT
  licence. The pinned release in `scanner_agent/tool_pins.env`.

